From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Shared loot inside a group; stand-ins for characters alive in other players' worlds

- loot.lua: what a member takes from a container or corpse (gold, ingredients, potions, lockpicks, probes, repair tools,
  ammunition; with a second setting plain weapons and armor) is removed from the other members' copies. Removal only, never
  scripted/enchanted/generated items, keys, books; the receiver decides what is shareable. Waiting removals are saved.
- proxies.lua: players outside the group list the characters around them (pubactors, relayed only to the same cell and
  outside the party); after an actor has been gone from our world for five minutes another world's copy stands in,
  labelled with its owner. Hits and kills stay local; at most eight; a cap on the records it can create.
- relay: loot (party only) and pubactors (same cell, not party) with validation and rate limits
- settings: shared loot, shared loot gear, other worlds' stand-ins
- loot_test.lua, standins_test.lua, relay tests, a real-server check

